","flags":[],"questionId":"cnm_269_q4","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"parallel-segments","label":"Find the missing part, then the whole","methodDirectNodeIds":{"parallel-segments":["cnm_269"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_269"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":2,"alignmentIds":["alignment:0183b589b25939b15f769b22"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"C (2√2 square centimeters)","reason":"Take A=(0,0,0), B=(3,0,0), D=(0,3,0), C=(3,3,0), and E=(0,0,6). Then P=(2,0,2), Q=(0,2,2), and R=(1,1,4). The midpoint M of PQ is (1,1,2), so RM=2 is perpendicular to PQ, whose length is 2√2. The area is (1/2)(2√2)(2)=2√2.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_269"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2019_AMC_12B_Q18","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"parallel-sections","label":"Similar horizontal square sections","methodDirectNodeIds":{"parallel-sections":["cnm_269","cnm_174"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_269","cnm_174"]},{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"parallel-square-section","label":"A parallel square section","methodDirectNodeIds":{"parallel-square-section":["cnm_269","cnm_185","cnm_174","cnm_p148"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_269","cnm_185","cnm_174","cnm_p148"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"alignmentIds":["alignment:0183b589b25939b15f769b22"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"C: 4:1","reason":"After cancelling the shared cut, the two remaining boundary lengths are equal and sum to 3+9+4+6=22, so each is 11. The leg portions next to the base 3 sum to 8, while those next to the base 9 sum to 2. Parallel-line proportionality gives the ratio 8:2=4:1 on each leg.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_269"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1957_AMC_12_Q49","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_055","cnm_p185","cnm_p186"],"id":"perimeter-balance","label":"Cancel the shared boundary","methodDire