gle area. The medians AG in ABF and EG in EBF give [ABG]=[AFG] and [EBG]=[EFG], hence [ABE]=[AFE]. Since AF/AC=1/3, [AFE]=[ACE]/3. Triangles ABE and ACE have the same altitude to BC, so BE:EC=1:3.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_269"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1971_AMC_12_Q26","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"parallel-line-similarity","label":"Parallel-line similarity","methodDirectNodeIds":{"parallel-line-similarity":["cnm_269","cnm_271","cnm_272"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_269","cnm_271","cnm_272"]},{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_055","cnm_p210","cnm_067"],"id":"parallel-segment-comparison","label":"Create proportional segments with a parallel line","methodDirectNodeIds":{"parallel-segment-comparison":["cnm_268","cnm_269"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_268","cnm_269","cnm_055","cnm_p210","cnm_067"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":3,"alignmentIds":["alignment:0183b589b25939b15f769b22"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"A (1/5)","reason":"Let S = [BDF]. Then [CDF] = 2S. Since BE is a median and [AEF] = [CEF], [ABF] = 3S. Thus [ABD] = 4S and [ABC] = 12S. Consequently [BCE] = 6S and [FDCE] = 5S, giving the ratio 1/5.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_269"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1980_AMC_12_Q21","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"id":"parallel-midsegment","label":"Construct a parallel midsegment","nodeIds":["cnm_185","cnm_269","cnm_p148","cnm_p150"]},{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_055","cnm_110","cnm_112","cnm_268","cnm_p185"],"id":"solution:parallel-midsegment:f4dea1de9db3","label":"Use a midsegment to locate F","methodDirectNodeIds":{"parallel-midsegment":["cnm_185","cnm_269","cnm_p148","cnm_p150"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_185","cnm_269","cnm_p148","cnm_p150","cnm_055","cnm_110","cnm_112","cnm_268","cnm_p185"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":3,"alignmentIds":["alignment:0183b589b25939b15f769b22"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"C: 7, with minimum PQ = 120/17 ≈ 7.059","reason":"Let O be the diagonal intersection. Then OA=8, OB=15, AB=17, and PQ=ON. The perpendicular from O meets AB internally, giving minimum ON=(8·15)/17=120/17, closest to 7.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_269"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2003_AMC_12B_Q22","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"quadratic-projection-lengths","label":"Projection ratios and quadratic minimum","methodDirectNodeIds":{"quadratic-projection-lengths":["cnm_269","cnm_235"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_269","cnm_235"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":3,"alignmentIds":["alignment:0183b589b25939b15f769b22"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D: √6 - √2","reason":"Take the tangent line as y = 0 and P = (0,1). Since PQ = 3 and QR = 5, their horizontal separations are √(9-1) = 2√2 and √(25-1) = 2√6. Hence Q = (2√2,2) and R = (2√2+2√6,3). The area is one half of |(2√2)(2) - (2√2+2√6)(1)|, which equals √6 - √2.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_269"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2016_AMC_10A_Q21","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"median-area","label":"Use a median and base-height area","methodDirectNodeIds":{"median-area":["cnm_269","cnm_113","cnm_p148"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_269","cnm_113","cnm_p148"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"alignmentIds":["alignment:0183b589b25939b15f769b22"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D: 18","reason":"Label the lower vertices A and B, the top vertex C, side points D on AC and E on BC, and the crossing P. Equal area-7 triangles give AP=PE, while DP:PB=3:7. Put u=[CPE] and v=[CPD]. Then u=v+3 and (u+7)/v=7/3. Solving gives v=15/2 and u=21/2, so the shaded area is u+v=18.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_269"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2006_AMC_10B_Q23","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"parallel-line-similarity","label":"Parallel-line similarity","methodDirectNodeIds":{"parallel-line-similarity":["cnm_269","cnm_271","cnm_272"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_269","cnm_271","cnm_272"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"alignmentIds":["alignment:0183b589b25939b15f769b22"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"C, 135/2","reason":"EA=8 and EB=2, so BF/AD=EB/EA=1/4 and BF=15/2. Also DG=15. The parallel sides are 6 units apart, giving area (15+15/2)·6/2=135/2.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_269"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2012_AMC_10B_Q19","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_055","cnm_268","cnm_p077"],"id":"parallel-segments-trapezoid","label":"Find the parallel sides of the trapezoid","methodDirectNodeIds":{"parallel-segments-trapezoid":["cnm_p149","cnm_269"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_p149","cnm_269","cnm_055","cnm_268","cnm_p077"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"alignmentIds":["alignment:0183b589b25939b15f769b22"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"A: 14.6 units","reason":"Relative to the whole triangle, the left shaded area is 1-(11/h)² and the right shaded area is ((h-5)/h)². Equality gives h²-121 = (h-5)², hence 10h = 146 and h = 14.6, which satisfies h > 11.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_269"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2023_AMC_8_Q24","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"equal-unshaded-areas","label":"Compare complementary areas","methodDirectNodeIds":{"equal-unshaded-areas":["cnm_269","cnm_p148","cnm_p149","cnm_042"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_269","cnm_p148","cnm_p149","cnm_042"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"alignmentIds":["alignment:0183b589b25939b15f769b22"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D, 95 minutes","reason":"The bottom, midline, and top sections have side length